@rob-linton - thank you for reporting this ... as you'll see, there's a patch ready to go, and we have some follow-up tidying to do.

It's not clear whether or when there will be a 25.0.4 containing the fix at the moment, but it will at-least be in 26.0.

In the meantime, with 25.x releases up-to 25.0.3, a possible workaround is to use a user-defined "nat" network.
